  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Let \\(r\\) be the result of doubling both the base and the exponent of \\(a^b,\\) \\(b\\ne0.\\) If \\(r\\) equals the product of \\(a^b\\) by \\(x^b,\\) then \\(x\\) equals:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(a\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(2a\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(4a\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(4\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1961-p9.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "We have \\[ r=(2a)^{2b}=(4a^2)^b \\] and also \\(r=a^bx^b=(ax)^b.\\) Thus \\(ax=4a^2,\\) so \\(x=4a.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Write the doubled expression as \\((2a)^{2b}\\)",
        "Express both sides as a single quantity raised to the \\(b\\)th power"
      ],
